<title>UK: Breakdown of C4 surplus payments to UK ITV network.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of C4 surplus payments to UK ITV network.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Independent Television Commission released the following breakdown on Thursday of 1996 payments to British Channel Three (ITV) licensees from Channel Four under the so-called funding formula.</p>
<p>    Company:					Share of surplus:</p>
<p>    Carlton			     12.9 million stg</p>
<p>    LWT				    9.5 million</p>
<p>    Central			     12.9 million</p>
<p>    Granada				9.3 million</p>
<p>    Yorkshire			    6.9 million</p>
<p>    Meridian			     9.6 million</p>
<p>    HTV				    5.8 million</p>
<p>    Scottish			     4.8 million</p>
<p>    Anglia				 5.8 million</p>
<p>    Tyne Tees			    2.6 million</p>
<p>    Westcountry			  1.6 million</p>
<p>    Ulster				 174,237</p>
<p>    Grampian			     113,255</p>
<p>    Border				  52,271</p>
<p>    Channel				 34,848</p>
<p>    GMTV				   5.1 million</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8793</p>
</text>
